the column u corresponding to s`\n> `Cancel out the row u corresponding to s`\n> `Add edge v-u to the tree`\n\nSo, at the next step of Prim's algorithm, we consider the smallest unselected distance over all marked columns ($v_1$, and $v_2$). The smallest value is $3$ at the intersection of row $v_4$ and column $v_1$.\n\nWe cancel out the row $v_4$ and add $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}v_1-v_4}$ of length $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}3}$ to the tree.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$<