\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$v_6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\">$6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\color{lightgrey}-$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"left\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"><div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Added edges</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Length</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$v_1 - v_4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$v_1 - v_2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$v_2 - v_3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$7$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$v_3 - v_6$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$v_6 - v_5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe total weight of the resulting minimum spanning tree is\n\n$$\n3 + 10 + 7 + 6 + 2 = 28\n$$"] [17592186110373 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$x$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$4$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>$f(x)$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$25$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?"] [17592186110529 :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality\n\n$$\nP(x) \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x)$. We can do this using the rational roots theorem. According to this theorem, the possible rational roots of $P(x)$ are\n\n$$\n\\pm \\dfrac{1}{2}, \\pm \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\pm 1, \\pm 3\n$$\n\nWe're given that the polynomial has at least one integer root, and so the list of possible integer roots is\n\n$$\n\\pm 1, \\pm 3\n$$\n\nLet's now test each of the above options until we find a root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1) &= -2(1)^{3} - 7(1)^{2} - 2(1) + 3 - 8\\cdot \\\\\nP(-1) &= -2(-1)^{3} - 7(-1)^{2} - 2(-1) + 3 = 0✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $x=-1$ is a root of $P(x)$, and so $(x+1)$ is a factor of $f(x)$ by the factor theorem.\n\nNow, let's use synthetic division to factor $P(x)$. We get the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$x^3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$x^2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$x^1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$x^0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"solid\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\">$\\color{red}-1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$-7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"solid\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"solid\">$\\color{gray}\\downarrow$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"solid\">$2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"solid\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"solid\">$-3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-top=\"none\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\" data-border-left=\"none\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$-2$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$-5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"Moccasin\" data-border-right=\"none\" data-border-bottom=\"none\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(x) &= (x + 1)(-2x^{2} - 5x + 3) \\\\\n&= - (x + 1)(2x^{2} + 5x - 3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the highest-degree factor is now quadratic, we can continue factoring using the usual methods. This gives\n\n$$\nP(x) =-(x+1)(2x-1)(x+3)\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $3$ simple roots,\n\n$$\nx=-3,-1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](images/a8/a831d09dbbe0f567bfe1bc06b79649f026e334ddec857362dcf7747bcce8abf7.png)\n\nSince\n\n$$\nP(x) \\leq 0\n$$\n\nwhen the curve $y=P(x)$ is below $x$-axis or touches this axis, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\in [-3,-1] \\cup \\left[\\dfrac{1}{2}, \\infty \\right)\n$$"] [17592186110543 :question/problem "Among $85$ surveyed cinema visitors,\n\n- $15$ men and $21$ women like crime movies,\n- $12$ women don't like crime movies.\n\nCopy and complete the joint frequency table below, and use this to determine the total number of men surveyed.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Like Crime Movies</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Don't Like Crime Movies</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table></div>\n\n"] [17592186110543 :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we can fill in part of the table as follows:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Like Crime Movies</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Don't Like Crime Movies</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFor a given joint frequency table:\n\n- the sum of the joint frequencies in any row/column equals the marginal frequency for that row/column, and\n- the sum of the marginal frequencies in the \"Totals\" row/column equals the total $(85)$.\n\nTherefore, filling in the remaining rows/columns, including the totals, we get the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Like Crime Movies</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Don't Like Crime Movies</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$15$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$37$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}52}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$21$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$33$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$36$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$49$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, $52$ men were surveyed."] [17592186110544 :question/problem "\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">German</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Spanish</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">French</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Boys</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Girls</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$t$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$w$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$29$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nThe frequency table above describes some children's preferences for learning a second language. Determine the value of $w + y + z$."] [17592186110544 :question/worked-solution "For each row/column in a joint frequency table:\n\n- the sum of the joint frequencies equals the marginal frequency (or total) for that row/column, and\n- the sum of the marginal frequencies in the totals row/column equals the total $(85)$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each row/column:\n\n- Looking at the first row, there are $44$ boys in total.\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">German</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Spanish</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">French</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Boys</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Girls</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals </th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$t$ </td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$w$ </td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$29$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore:\n$$\n\\displaystyle 8 + x + 14|= 44; 22 + x|= 44; x|= 44 - 22; x|= 22\n$$\nWe add this value to our table.\n- Looking at the third column, we see that there are $29$ children who prefer to learn French.\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">German</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Spanish</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">French</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Boys</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Girls</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$y$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$z$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals </th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$t$ </td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$w$ </td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#FCF3CF\">$29$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore:\n$$\n\\displaystyle 14 + y|= 29; y|= 29 - 14; y|= 15\n$$\nWe add this value to our table.\n\nBy similar reasoning, we can deduce the following:\n\n- Considering the number of children who prefer to learn German, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle t|= 8 + 12 = 20.\n$$\n- Considering the number of children who prefer to learn Spanish, we get\n$$\n\\displaystyle w|= 22 + 14 = 36.\n$$\n- Since there are $85$ children in total, we have\n$$\n\\displaystyle 44 + z|= 85; z|= 85 - 44; z|= 41.\n$$\n\nOur completed frequency table is as follows:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">German</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Spanish</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">French</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Boys</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$22$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$44$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Girls</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$12$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$14$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}15}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}41}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}36}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$29$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$85$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nw + y + z = 36 + 15 + 41 = 92\n$$"] [17592186110545 :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we can fill in part of the table as follows:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Swimming</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Tanning</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Volleyball</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$45$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nNote that we have let $x$ equal the number of men who plan to prefer to tan.\n\nFor a given joint frequency table:\n\n- the sum of the joint frequencies in any row/column equals the marginal frequency for that row/column, and\n- the sum of the marginal frequencies in the \"Totals\" row/column equals the total $(100)$.\n\nFilling in some more rows/columns using this idea, we get the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Swimming</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Tanning</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Volleyball</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$45$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$3x$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$55$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$43$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$27$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFrom the second row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n23 + x + 3x &= 55 \\\\\n4x + 23 &= 55 \\\\\n4x &= 32 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{32}{4} \\\\\nx &= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing this result and filling in the rest of the table, we finally arrive at the following:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-border-top=\"solid\" data-border-left=\"solid\"></td>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Swimming</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Tanning</th>\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Volleyball</th>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Women</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$20$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$19$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{red}6}$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$45$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-fill=\"#F2F4F4\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Men</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$23$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$24$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$55$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\" data-cell-weight=\"bold\">Totals</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$43$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$27$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#EBF5FB\">$30$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$100$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFinally, we conclude that $6$ women prefer volleyball."] [17592186110901 :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(μ, 1)$ with $P(X < 4) = 0.8413$, find $μ$.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.00$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.01$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.02$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1.0$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8413$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8438$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8461$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1.1$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8643$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8665$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8686$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$1.2$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8849$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8869$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.8888$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186110902 :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(μ, 10^{2})$ with $P(X \\ge 2) = 0.3821$, find $μ$.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.00$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.01$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.02$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.2$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.5793$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.5832$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.5871$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.3$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6179$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6217$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6255$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.4$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6554$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6591$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.6628$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [17592186110903 :question/problem "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(0, σ^{2})$ and $P(X \\le - 4) = 0.3446$, find $σ$.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$z$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.00$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.01$</th>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$0.02$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$-0.6$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.2743$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.2709$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0.2676$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$-0.5$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"